  "interpretations": {
    "authentication": "The API declares bearerAuth but supplies no global/operation security requirement. The separate official authentication and signing instructions require Bearer plus HMAC-SHA512.",
    "request": "Publisher sorting recurses objects but not object elements inside arrays. HMAC-SHA512 covers lowercase path excluding query, optional body HMAC, and original ten-digit timestamp.",
    "callback": "HMAC-SHA512 covers configured registered URL, HMAC of JSON.stringify(event.data), and original timestamp. Envelope event label is not authenticated. URL exact/lowercase convention is explicitly configured.",
    "writes": "No idempotency-key parameter is declared. An uncertain mutation uses original readback, never an invented retry assurance.",
    "units": "Original provider amounts and exact numeric lexemes are retained. Domain controls use documented minor units and explicit conversion evidence for ledger asset amounts.",
    "stellar": "No Paycashless Stellar endpoint, deployed contract, issuer or custody account is declared in this original API. Horizon and allocation bindings are selected explicitly."
  }
